- Story & Context: Young Sofia asks her grandmother why the spice market smells like burnt rubber and ozone, a confession prompted by a sudden power surge in their barge’s makeshift sound system. The grandmother admits the music isn't played to please the crowd, but to keep the hungry river spirits from boarding the boats to steal the morning meal. "Salt the rhythm until the ghosts turn back," Sofia sang, her voice trembling as the synths began to pitch-shift wildly downward.
