Track 3: The Silt-Layer Coefficient
- Story & Context: Local merchants gather at the floating wharf of San Jeronimo to hear the final, legendary set of the season where the music purportedly causes the tide to rise three inches. The performance remains a point of historical contention, as critics argue the bass was merely a sonic frequency designed to shift the mud beneath the piers. "Logic cannot measure the depth of the lamento," the village elder proclaimed, pointing at the water line that had mysteriously climbed over the docking boards during the track's crescendo.
